  "texts": {
    "preamble": "State vs Bhanwar Lal & Ors on 13 September, 2017 Author: Pushpendra Singh Bhati Bench: Pushpendra Singh Bhati High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan At Jodhpur S.B. Criminal Misc(Pet.) No. 3343 / 2016 State of Rajasthan ----Petitioner Versus 1. Bhanwar Lal Rathore S/o Puna Ram Ji, Seller & Owner of M/s Sharda Traders, Hanuman Chowk, Post Office Road- Sumerpur ( Pali) 2. Mahesh Kumar Agarwal S/o Jagdish Agarwal, Partner- M/s Chetan Industry, f 83 Kesarganj, Riico Industrial Area, Shivganj, Sirohi 3. Smt. Sunita Agarwal W/o Shiv Kumar Agarwal, Partner- M/s Chetan Industry, f 83 Kesarganj, Riico Industrial Area, Shivganj, Sirohi 4. M/s Chetan Industry, F 83 Kesarganj, RIICO Industrial Area, Shivganj, Sirohi ----Respondents _____________________________________________________ For Petitioner(s) : Mr. KK Rawal PP for the State.",
    "facts": "2. The accused respondents were discharged under Sections 7/16 of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act on 8.10.2013 and the revision petition was preferred and the same was also dismissed on 4.06.2016.",
    "arguments": "The some and substance of both the orders below is that the Section 32(i) in the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act which reads as follows: \"Explanation(vi)--\"Wholesale package\" means a package containing:-- (a) a number of retail packages, where such first mentioned packages are intended for sale, distribution or delivery to an intermediary and are not intended for sale direct to any consumer, or (b) a commodity of food sold to an intermediary in bulk to enable such intermediary to sell, distribute or deliver such commodity of food to the consumer in smaller quantities.\" 4.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "The some and substance of both the orders below is that the Section 32(i) in the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act which reads as follows: \"Explanation(vi)--\"Wholesale package\" means a package containing:-- (a) a number of retail packages, where such first mentioned packages are intended for sale, distribution or delivery to an intermediary and are not intended for sale direct to any consumer, or (b) a commodity of food sold to an intermediary in bulk to enable such intermediary to sell, distribute or deliver such commodity of food to the consumer in smaller quantities.\" 4."
